From: Fathom <fathom@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] MIPS: ingenic: hifiwalker-h2: number the MMC hosts

With Wi-Fi on MSC1 there are two MMC hosts, and without aliases each takes
the next free number as it probes: now and then the Wi-Fi host comes first,
the microSD card becomes mmc1 (mmcblk1), and anything that looks for
mmcblk0 misses it (the boot report waited 10 s and gave up). The card's
slot is always mmc0 now, its card mmcblk0; Wi-Fi is mmc1.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/arch/mips/boot/dts/ingenic/hifiwalker-h2.dts
+++ b/arch/mips/boot/dts/ingenic/hifiwalker-h2.dts
@@ -18,6 +18,12 @@
 / {
 	compatible = "hifiwalker,h2", "ingenic,x1000";
 	model = "HiFi Walker H2";
+
+	/* the microSD card always mmc0 (mmcblk0), Wi-Fi mmc1 */
+	aliases {
+		mmc0 = &msc0;
+		mmc1 = &msc1;
+	};
 
 	memory {
 		device_type = "memory";
